// Brake throttle override (BTO): the brake beats the accelerator. After the
// idea in NHTSA's proposal to amend FMVSS No. 124 (2012), written after
// unintended acceleration cases where a stuck or trapped pedal held the
// throttle open while the driver braked.
//
// Brake down: throttle to 0, whatever the pedal says. And once the override
// has taken, it holds until the accelerator is released -- lifting the brake
// with the pedal still down must not surge the car forward.
//
// A cycle is a sample. Pins are the board's business.

#analog   Pedal:8 unsigned in 0     // accelerator, %
#digital  Brake in 1
#variable Bto:1 = 0                 // the override has taken
#variable Throttle:8 unsigned = 0   // requested throttle, %

#annotate varp reach "Throttle' == 100"
// Goals never reached, for the solver:
//     Brake && Throttle' != 0                 the brake always wins
//     Bto && Pedal > 0 && Throttle' != 0      no surge when the brake lifts

Bto = 1 ? Brake && Pedal > 0
Bto = 0 ? !Brake && Pedal == 0

Throttle = Pedal ? !Brake && !Bto
Throttle = 0 ? Brake || Bto
